    <innerclass refid="class_cycle_dynamics" prot="public">CycleDynamics</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Defines the <ref refid="class_cycle_dynamics" kindref="compound">CycleDynamics</ref> class, which implements periodic non–mass-based dynamics. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="class_cycle_dynamics" kindref="compound">CycleDynamics</ref> class models a repeating sequence of values (a cycle) that influences dynamic traits or ecological processes within the Weaver simulation framework. These dynamics do not depend on biomass; instead, they follow a discrete periodic pattern that updates at each time step.</para>
<para>Typical uses include seasonal activity cycles, periodic physiological adjustments, or cyclical environmental effects. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
